{#
    Twelve months of spend, drawn from the forecast.

    The design's chart plotted income against expenses. A subscription tracker
    has no income, so this is what it does have: each renewal in the month it
    actually falls, with scheduled price changes and trial conversions applied
    from their own dates. It is the same call the Forecast page makes, so the
    two screens cannot disagree about a month.

    The chart itself is `partials/spend_chart.twig`, which the analytics
    screen's spending trajectory also renders — one payload, one picture, drawn
    in two places.
#}
{% import 'partials/spend_chart.twig' as trend %}

<section class="card chart-card">
    <header class="card-header">
        <h2>{{ t('dashboard.spend_chart') }}</h2>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="/forecast">{{ t('nav.forecast') }}</a>
    </header>

    {{ trend.spend_chart(
        chart,
        'dashboard-spend-data',
        t('dashboard.spend_chart_alt', {'currency': chart.currency})
    ) }}
</section>
